Take a fresh chunk when the adjacent free run no longer matches

kmem_get_additional_meta samples the adjacent free run, then the code populates the
metadata around the watermark, which rewrites those markers.  The equality checked
afterwards can then never hold, so kmem_get_new_chunk returns NULL on every call and
the pointer range never gets a chunk.  Print the four numbers and drop the merge
instead, so the allocation proceeds at the watermark.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
index 2927d4b..8889e1c 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -2891,7 +2891,16 @@ kmem_get_new_chunk(
 			if (adj_free_meta->km_page_marker != KMEM_META_FREE ||
 			    kmem_get_free_chunk_len(adj_free_meta) !=
 			    meta_req - meta_num) {
-				return NULL;
+				/*
+				 * nio: the adjacent free run was sampled before the populate above
+				 * rewrote the surrounding metadata, so the equality can no longer
+				 * hold and every call gives up here.  Drop the merge and take a
+				 * fresh chunk at the watermark instead of failing forever.
+				 */
+				printf("\nA q=%u n=%u f=%u m=%x\n", meta_req, meta_num,
+				    kmem_get_free_chunk_len(adj_free_meta),
+				    adj_free_meta->km_page_marker);
+				adj_free_meta = NULL;
 			}
 		}
 
